a new alone in the dark game is coming  returning the series all the way back to  its 1992 roots with a reboot of the game  that helped create the survival horror  genre thq nordic announced the game  during its 2022 game showcase and gave  gamespot an early hands-off look at  alone in the dark which it calls a  reimagining of and a love letter to the  original 3d horror game the rebooted  title is a third-person horror  experience that takes a page from more  recent entries in the genre like  resident evil 4 5 and 6 and dead space  if you're not familiar the original  alone in the dark was set in the 1920s  american south and followed one of two  characters as they tried to escape a  monster-filled mansion called derceto  manor a lot of the things we've come to  think of as survival horror like  dangerous fights with monsters that  leave you feeling underpowered and  solving puzzles as you explore are major  elements of the original game there have  been several games in the alone in the  dark series since the first was released  but the latest game is returning to what  made the original a classic while  updating those elements for modern  audiences swedish developer pieces  interactive is making the new alone in  the dark which also centers on dursetto  manor in the 20s and the original's two  main playable characters private  detective edward carnby and emily  hartwood you'll choose which character  to play at the start of the game like in  the original but this time edward and  emily's stories aren't exactly the same  so to get the full picture of what  happens in alone in the dark you'll  probably want to play it twice dursetto  manor has been recast as a mental  hospital for rich patients as in the  original game the characters arrive  looking for information about emily's  uncle jeremy hartwood but instead of  trying to uncover details about the  mansion owner's suicide they're  attempting to find him after jeremy sent  a strange letter to emily dercetto isn't  the only setting you'll visit either  there are new locations that make up the  game including a spooky alternate  dimension world you'll visit through  portals and which seems to be full of  monsters combat is a major part of the  game and you'll use both firearms and  melee weapons to fight some hideous  twisted monsters footage we saw included  pistols and shotguns but it sounds like  you'll also have to defend yourself with  whatever objects you can grab  you'll also face monsters you can't  easily kill which might mean you'll have  to run away instead of standing your  ground  the game's monsters are designed by  artist guy davis who worked on gears of  war 4 and movies such as the shape of  water nightmare alley and pacific rim  story is also a big component of the new  alone in the dark with amnesia the dark  descent and soma writer mikkel hedberg  penning the reimagined version of the  game's tale hedberg said during thq's  presentation that the story will be more  active than the original expect  cinematic cutscenes and voice dialogue  in addition to notes letters and other  items you'll find as you explore  dursetto manor and the rest of the world  according to thq though the game will  see you fighting monsters and  occasionally running from threats it's  taking a different tack than other  survival horror games while most tend to  focus on a more terror experience alone  in the dark is trying to explore other  aspects of the horror genre the original  had a fairly lovecraftian story with a  lot of dense heavy atmosphere and  psychological dread that atmospheric  brand of horror is something developers  are focusing on for this new game and  while you'll definitely fight horrific  creatures combat may not be the main  thrust of the game alone in the dark is  coming to playstation 5 xbox series xns  and pc thq said the game has been in the  works since late 2019 and is currently  right around an alpha state but no  release date has yet been set a teaser  featuring grace a returning character  from alone in the dark 2 will be  playable at gamescom later this month  and now let's leave you with some more  gameplay so you can get a sense of alone  in the dark for yourself  [Music]  [Applause]  so  you
 

